WEBVTT

00:06.260 --> 00:09.460
Now that finals are over, it's time to turn over a new leaf.

00:11.740 --> 00:12.860
Mr. Kazuki Sendou

00:18.310 --> 00:19.870
Ikumi Tachikawa

00:21.210 --> 00:24.150
Miss Tachikawa... She's so earnest.

00:24.620 --> 00:26.640
She goes to the trouble of writing to someone like me.

00:28.590 --> 00:32.520
"Keep it up, and good luck on your new issue for the summer."

00:39.900 --> 00:43.460
<i>Just be you and don't change.</i>
<i>Kimi no Mama de Kawaranaide</i>

00:44.000 --> 00:47.140
<i>You're more precious to me than anyone.</i>
<i>Dare Yori mo Taisetsu na</i>

00:47.140 --> 00:50.700
<i>You have a great, sparkling dream...</i>
<i>Ohki na Yume Kagayakaseta</i>

00:50.910 --> 00:53.970
<i>...and you're my one and only friend.</i>
<i>Tada Hitori no Tomodachi</i>

00:54.250 --> 00:57.850
<i>It just doesn't get across...</i>
<i>Nani o Shite mo Tsutawarazu</i>

00:57.850 --> 01:01.420
<i>It's just not working right at all.</i>
<i>Umaku Ikanai Bakari de</i>

01:01.420 --> 01:04.790
<i>But even I and everyone else...</i>
<i>Watashi Datte Dare Datte</i>

01:04.990 --> 01:08.520
<i>... have times like that.</i>
<i>Atarimae ni Aru Koto</i>

01:08.590 --> 01:12.000
<i>Those things that don't return to your heart.</i>
<i>Mune no Naka ni Kaeranai</i>

01:12.200 --> 01:15.570
<i>But even those words and feelings...</i>
<i>Omoi mo Kotoba mo Itsuka</i>

01:15.770 --> 01:20.170
<i>... will come back in time someday...</i>
<i>Jikan ga Tateba Modotte Kuru kara</i>

01:20.370 --> 01:23.310
<i>... before you know it.</i>
<i>Shiranai Uchi ni</i>

01:23.610 --> 01:29.510
<i>There's only one thing you can do right now.</i>
<i>Ima Kimiga Dekiru Koto wa Hitotsu</i>

01:29.880 --> 01:36.580
<i>Just accept it and go with it.</i>
<i>Sono Mama Ukeirete Yukou</i>

01:37.260 --> 01:41.260
<i>Just be you and stay true to yourself.</i>
<i>Kimi no Mama de Itsuwarazu ni</i>

01:41.260 --> 01:44.430
<i>Take a little break.</i>
<i>Sukoshi Hitoyasumi Shite</i>

01:44.430 --> 01:48.170
<i>Take your impatience and your hardships...</i>
<i>Aseru Kimochi Kurushii Koto</i>

01:48.170 --> 01:51.430
<i>...and turn them into your strengths.</i>
<i>Kimi no Power ni Kaete</i>

01:51.500 --> 01:55.270
<i>Just be you and don't change.</i>
<i>Kimi no Mama de Kawaranaide</i>

01:55.640 --> 01:58.740
<i>You're more precious to me than anyone.</i>
<i>Dare Yori mo Taisetsu na</i>

01:58.740 --> 02:02.340
<i>You have a great, sparkling dream...</i>
<i>Ohki na Yume Kagayakaseta</i>

02:02.550 --> 02:05.450
<i>...and you're my one and only friend.</i>
<i>Tada Hitori no Tomodachi</i>

02:08.450 --> 02:15.220
THE

02:08.450 --> 02:15.220
UNCERTAIN

02:08.450 --> 02:15.220
FUTURE

02:19.730 --> 02:22.030
Listen up, this is a Parent
Student Teacher meeting.

02:22.370 --> 02:25.930
It'll be the final meeting regarding your future after graduation,

02:26.140 --> 02:28.400
so make sure you give that to someone in your family.

02:34.510 --> 02:36.570
So, what are you going to do, Kazuki?

02:36.650 --> 02:37.580
About what?

02:37.580 --> 02:39.680
What you're going to do after graduation.

02:39.750 --> 02:41.910
I'll go to college, of course.

02:42.150 --> 02:43.190
Where?

02:43.190 --> 02:45.890
Where? Our school automatically gets us into college, remember?

02:47.390 --> 02:49.360
Is it okay to leave it at that?

02:51.700 --> 02:56.260
Is it okay to just go to the college affiliated with our school?

02:56.430 --> 02:58.100
What are you talking about, all of a sudden?

02:58.300 --> 03:02.040
College directly affects your employment and things, right?

03:02.340 --> 03:05.440
It means a certain part of your life will be set at that point.

03:05.540 --> 03:07.240
Well, that's true.

03:07.750 --> 03:10.940
Maybe we should think more carefully about our future...

03:11.180 --> 03:14.380
...and about what we want to do in life.

03:14.850 --> 03:17.450
You know, though?
You talk about the future,

03:17.590 --> 03:20.820
but I just don't get it.
It doesn't feel real.

03:21.290 --> 03:24.420
Besides, if you want to try for other colleges,

03:24.500 --> 03:26.900
you have to study for entrance exams.

03:27.100 --> 03:28.730
That would be such a pain.

03:30.670 --> 03:33.800
I think it's okay to just go to the affiliated college...

03:33.940 --> 03:38.140
...and then think about the future once you're there, you know?

03:40.350 --> 03:41.540
That's true.

03:41.680 --> 03:42.580
See?

03:42.580 --> 03:44.910
Yeah, you're right, Kazuki.

04:02.900 --> 04:04.130
The future...

04:06.270 --> 04:09.610
Am I going to end up wearing a suit and going to work,

04:09.610 --> 04:11.410
swaying in a jam-packed train?

04:12.180 --> 04:16.050
That sounds so fake. I can't even imagine myself doing that.

04:17.750 --> 04:22.210
But... I guess Mizuki's giving this some serious thought.

04:23.490 --> 04:25.150
I wonder if everyone's like that?

04:25.360 --> 04:28.920
Naturally! Yes! Of course!

04:29.690 --> 04:32.600
Without a detailed blueprint showing us the way to the future,

04:32.760 --> 04:37.070
our Brother 2's plan to conquer the world could not exist!

04:37.470 --> 04:39.300
No, that's not what I meant.

04:39.470 --> 04:43.000
What I want to know is about your own personal future...

04:43.140 --> 04:45.040
It is the same thing, my brother!

04:45.680 --> 04:48.770
The future of Brother 2 lies upon our shoulders.

04:48.980 --> 04:52.970
In other words, the future of Brother 2 is our future!

04:53.180 --> 04:56.350
Our future is the future of Brother 2!

04:57.090 --> 05:00.080
H-hold on a minute.
I already told you, I'm not...

05:00.290 --> 05:03.030
Damn it, do you still not get it, after everything I've said?!

05:03.030 --> 05:04.330
CURRY BREAD

05:04.660 --> 05:08.060
Comrade Kazuki, what in the world do you think this is?

05:08.170 --> 05:09.630
A curry bread, I think?

05:09.900 --> 05:11.070
That's right!

05:11.070 --> 05:13.630
This is indeed but a simple curry bread.

05:13.740 --> 05:17.470
However, if this curry bread became a food that saw widespread consumption...

05:17.540 --> 05:19.940
...and transcended nationality, race, and religion,

05:20.040 --> 05:23.710
it would have truly succeeded in conquering the world!

05:25.850 --> 05:29.150
Our Brother 2 will also be like the curry bread!

05:29.450 --> 05:32.480
Currently, we have just budded and sprouted our first leaves,

05:32.720 --> 05:35.320
but soon, we will blossom into a large, beautiful flower.

05:35.690 --> 05:37.390
W-we will?

05:37.900 --> 05:40.390
Do not underestimate the curry bread!

05:40.700 --> 05:43.530
He who ridicules the curry bread will be made sorry by the curry bread!

05:43.670 --> 05:47.260
He who controls the curry bread will control the world!

05:47.770 --> 05:50.440
So? Are you going to buy that or aren't you?

05:50.540 --> 05:51.310
What?

05:51.310 --> 05:54.580
Everyone's waiting in line, so hurry up and make up your mind.

06:02.120 --> 06:04.590
I'm planning on joining the broadcast research society.

06:05.460 --> 06:07.860
Come to think of it, you want to be in the TV business, don't you?

06:08.760 --> 06:10.820
What are you planning to do?

06:10.900 --> 06:12.730
I guess a car comes first for me.

06:12.730 --> 06:13.930
A car?

06:14.000 --> 06:15.870
I'll attend a training facility during spring break...

06:15.870 --> 06:18.800
...and when I get into college,
I'll tell my dad and get my car.

06:19.200 --> 06:21.410
You gotta have your own way to get around in college.

06:21.410 --> 06:22.670
Yeah, that's true.

06:22.140 --> 06:23.800
I want a car, too.

06:24.610 --> 06:26.310
My future?

06:26.580 --> 06:27.350
Yeah.

06:27.350 --> 06:29.840
Well, I guess I'll take over the family business.

06:30.110 --> 06:31.220
Family business?

06:31.220 --> 06:32.770
A hot spring inn.

06:32.880 --> 06:33.820
Oh.

06:34.220 --> 06:36.480
I promised my mom and pop,

06:36.620 --> 06:39.850
and I can't let the inn go to waste with my generation.

06:39.920 --> 06:40.890
Besides...

06:40.990 --> 06:41.820
Besides?

06:42.760 --> 06:44.750
I like that place.

06:45.460 --> 06:51.270
Includin' my silly mom and pop, the employees, and the rundown buildin'.

06:52.270 --> 06:54.930
And that's why I'm puttin' everythin' I've got into it right now.

06:55.210 --> 06:57.570
Into comics and into doujin work.

06:59.210 --> 07:02.670
Right now? Are you going to quit doujin work?

07:02.980 --> 07:04.280
Well, someday.

07:04.750 --> 07:06.340
But, why?

07:07.020 --> 07:09.650
There's nothin' to be surprised about. I'm the same as you.

07:09.790 --> 07:10.590
What?

07:10.590 --> 07:14.290
When I lose the desire to draw comics and make doujinshi,

07:14.360 --> 07:15.730
I'll quit right then.

07:15.730 --> 07:17.390
That's all there is to it.

07:20.230 --> 07:23.000
But well, that's still far ahead.

07:26.240 --> 07:30.900
As long as there are people lookin' forward to my comics and doujinshi,

07:31.040 --> 07:33.100
I'll never lose the desire to keep doin' it.

07:33.280 --> 07:35.540
Even if it's just one person.

07:38.550 --> 07:41.250
Well, the future's the future.
The present's the present.

07:41.390 --> 07:43.860
You gotta do what you wanna do now, while you still can.

07:44.390 --> 07:47.850
So, what's up, anyway? Suddenly bringin' up stuff about the future?

07:47.960 --> 07:49.790
Oh, no, well...just sort of...

07:50.360 --> 07:51.590
It's okay, never mind.

07:54.930 --> 07:57.900
<i>Taishi's a different story,</i> <i>but everyone, even Yuu,</i>

07:58.000 --> 08:01.230
<i>is thinking seriously</i> <i>about their own future.</i>

08:09.280 --> 08:10.480
Chisa...

08:14.050 --> 08:16.850
She looks busy. I guess it's the end of the year.

08:18.520 --> 08:23.360
I'll bet Chisa's also thinking about the future.

08:23.730 --> 08:26.460
Am I sure I'm okay with how things are?

08:26.530 --> 08:27.760
Hi there!

08:29.900 --> 08:30.940
Miss Reiko...

08:30.940 --> 08:32.530
Hi, hi!

08:33.640 --> 08:35.160
What are you doing here?

08:36.070 --> 08:38.570
Oh, that fish store is my friend's house.

08:38.710 --> 08:39.910
From cosplaying?

08:39.910 --> 08:42.880
Yup, I was here making arrangements for the winter Comi-Pa.

08:43.050 --> 08:44.610
You're going to be there too, right?

08:44.720 --> 08:46.310
What? Well, uh...

08:46.680 --> 08:47.810
Oh, yeah...

08:48.790 --> 08:51.290
Foreign Language Technical Institute

08:49.090 --> 08:52.660
Sheesh, didn't you already decide what school you're going to?

08:52.960 --> 08:55.150
This is going to determine my life.

08:55.360 --> 08:57.420
You have to look thoroughly into these things.

08:57.860 --> 08:59.630
But talk about a surprise.

08:59.800 --> 09:03.700
I never knew you were planning to go to a technical institute.

09:03.940 --> 09:07.740
I don't have a choice.
Our school's affiliated college...

09:07.740 --> 09:10.170
...won't let me become an interpreter.

09:10.540 --> 09:14.070
Besides, speak for yourself. You're going to a kinesiology college, right?

09:14.750 --> 09:17.240
I don't know if I'll get in yet, though.

09:17.350 --> 09:21.950
Kinesiology colleges have skills tests on top of academics, so it's tough.

09:22.320 --> 09:24.150
You're so lucky, Mizuki.

09:24.220 --> 09:25.250
What?

09:25.320 --> 09:27.960
You get to do what you want just by automatically...

09:27.960 --> 09:30.020
...advancing into our affiliated college, right?

09:30.090 --> 09:31.150
Oh, yeah.

09:31.230 --> 09:35.960
Man, if only our college was stronger in languages.

09:36.200 --> 09:38.400
Then I wouldn't have to go to all this trouble.

09:39.840 --> 09:40.910
I guess.

09:40.910 --> 09:43.000
Foreign Language Technical Institute

09:43.510 --> 09:45.170
My future?

09:45.740 --> 09:46.730
Yeah.

09:46.880 --> 09:49.450
I get it. You're a senior, aren't you?

09:49.450 --> 09:52.350
You've got graduation coming up, so you're getting worried.

09:52.680 --> 09:53.650
Something like that.

09:54.090 --> 09:57.420
I make costumes for cosplays, you know?

09:57.720 --> 10:01.820
I want to get into something fashion-related with those skills.

10:02.490 --> 10:07.060
Wow, you're still a junior, but you're already giving it serious thought.

10:07.470 --> 10:11.770
Oh? So what? Do I look like I don't think at all?

10:11.900 --> 10:13.930
What? No, that's not what I...

10:14.010 --> 10:17.700
I see, so you're treating me today, right?

10:17.910 --> 10:18.980
What?!

10:18.610 --> 10:19.970
Miss!

10:20.680 --> 10:22.150
I'm home.

10:21.610 --> 10:24.010
Oh, Kazuki, there's a letter for you.

10:26.550 --> 10:28.540
<i>Who would be sending me a letter?</i>

10:31.460 --> 10:33.690
Ikumi Tachikawa

10:32.120 --> 10:33.420
<i>Miss Tachikawa...</i>

10:39.660 --> 10:41.960
<i>"Greetings, Mr. Kazuki Sendou."</i>

10:42.470 --> 10:45.630
<i>"With the winter Comic</i>
<i>Party coming up shortly,</i>

10:45.740 --> 10:48.800
<i>"I am sure this letter will find</i> <i>you in the midst of writing for it.</i>

10:49.070 --> 10:52.640
<i>"I first saw your work at the</i> <i>spring exhibition and spot sale...</i>

10:52.640 --> 10:54.480
<i>"...and it was truly striking.</i>

10:55.050 --> 10:57.780
<i>"It lacked polish, but your</i> <i>originality was unrivaled...</i>

10:57.780 --> 11:00.950
<i>"...and that was something</i> <i>to be surprised about.</i>

11:01.150 --> 11:05.490
<i>"However, I was greatly disappointed</i> <i>with your summer Comi-Pa work.</i>

11:06.020 --> 11:09.930
<i>"But recently, you seem to</i> <i>have shown signs of recovery.</i>

11:10.060 --> 11:12.930
<i>"I am looking forward, from</i> <i>the depths of my heart,</i>

11:12.930 --> 11:16.770
<i>"to the completion of a</i> <i>piece that you wish to draw,</i>

11:16.770 --> 11:18.930
<i>"and to you releasing your</i> <i>work at the winter Comi-Pa.</i>

11:19.200 --> 11:20.900
<i>"Ikumi Tachikawa."</i>

11:24.010 --> 11:25.910
She's as earnest as ever.

11:26.040 --> 11:29.070
But I've quit doujin work...

11:29.650 --> 11:32.910
But, "recently showing signs of recovery"?

11:32.980 --> 11:34.680
What is she talking about?

11:38.790 --> 11:41.160
Who is this Miss Tachikawa, anyway?

11:43.530 --> 11:46.730
It seems like she reads my doujinshi, but...

11:52.640 --> 11:56.130
No way. That girl?
Writing letters like this?

11:59.280 --> 12:00.370
Oh, Mizuki...

12:00.650 --> 12:03.380
Hello? What? After school tomorrow?

12:04.250 --> 12:05.750
Do you have time?

12:05.750 --> 12:07.740
<i>I don't have any plans or anything.</i>

12:07.820 --> 12:09.690
Then, you wanna go to a presentation?

12:09.690 --> 12:10.690
<i>Presentation?</i>

12:10.690 --> 12:19.690
Hotel Management

12:10.690 --> 12:19.690
Technical Institute

12:10.690 --> 12:19.690
Travel Management

12:10.690 --> 12:19.690
Technical School

12:11.060 --> 12:12.220
Yeah.

12:12.220 --> 12:16.930
A technical institute is giving a presentation tomorrow evening.

12:17.130 --> 12:19.690
That is, only if you want to.

12:20.230 --> 12:23.130
Okay, sure. Then I'll see you tomorrow.

12:29.470 --> 12:31.070
Hotel Management

12:29.470 --> 12:31.070
Technical Institute

12:29.470 --> 12:31.070
Travel Management

12:29.470 --> 12:31.070
Technical School

12:44.320 --> 12:48.790
Yoyomori International Travel Institute

12:44.960 --> 12:48.130
At our school, we invite alumni from first-rate hotels...

12:48.130 --> 12:50.890
...and hotel employees who are currently in the industry, to give lectures.

12:51.460 --> 12:54.860
Our curriculum actually allows you to experience the business.

12:55.000 --> 12:57.660
The curriculum is held in high esteem, even among our industry peers.

12:57.870 --> 13:01.740
This results in our school's high employment rate after graduation.

13:02.370 --> 13:04.040
May I ask a question?

13:04.110 --> 13:05.180
Yes, go ahead.

13:05.180 --> 13:07.880
The pamphlet mentions a foreign student exchange program.

13:07.880 --> 13:09.400
How does it work?

13:09.480 --> 13:12.050
It is a student exchange program that we conduct every year...

13:12.050 --> 13:14.990
...between our school and partner schools overseas.

13:19.920 --> 13:24.620
I never knew you wanted to get into the travel or hotel business.

13:25.460 --> 13:29.030
But you did always say that you wanted to travel to different places,

13:29.130 --> 13:31.160
so I guess it's perfect, now that I think about it.

13:32.100 --> 13:36.010
You have to be able to speak
English to get those jobs, right?

13:36.070 --> 13:38.600
I bet it'll be tough, once you get into the school.

13:40.010 --> 13:42.080
Mizuki? Hey, are you listening?

13:42.080 --> 13:43.950
What? Oh, yeah.

13:44.180 --> 13:45.810
You've been acting weird.

13:45.880 --> 13:48.110
Y-you think so? It must be your imagination.

13:48.690 --> 13:51.950
If you've got a problem, don't hesitate to tell me about it.

13:52.220 --> 13:53.990
I don't have any problems...

13:55.660 --> 13:57.330
You know, if...

13:57.330 --> 14:02.430
If you and I end up going to different schools, what would you do?

14:02.430 --> 14:05.130
What would I do?
Well, it can't be helped.

14:05.270 --> 14:08.030
You have stuff you want to do, after all.

14:09.240 --> 14:11.640
That's true. You're right.

14:11.980 --> 14:13.950
A travel-related job, huh?

14:14.150 --> 14:17.210
It sounds tough, but I bet it'll be rewarding.

14:17.620 --> 14:21.250
It's great, Mizuki.
You know what your future goals are.

14:21.250 --> 14:22.380
It's not great.

14:22.450 --> 14:23.320
What?

14:23.320 --> 14:24.520
It's not great at all!

14:25.620 --> 14:30.150
Because I haven't thought at all about what I want to do with my future!

14:30.560 --> 14:34.460
But you're going to that school to find a job, right?

14:35.000 --> 14:36.830
That's not really what I have in mind.

14:37.300 --> 14:40.900
Then why did we attend today's presentation?

14:41.340 --> 14:42.670
That's because...

14:43.110 --> 14:45.170
You're really acting weird.

14:45.240 --> 14:46.730
You're lucky, Kazuki.

14:48.150 --> 14:50.480
You can decide on your future without agonizing about it.

14:51.150 --> 14:53.450
Reina wants to become an interpreter,

14:53.450 --> 14:55.940
and Chinami's aiming to become a P.E. teacher.

14:56.390 --> 15:00.880
Everyone has their goals, but I...

15:01.160 --> 15:04.690
When I think about what I want to do or what I want to be,

15:04.800 --> 15:07.060
I suddenly start feeling panicked, and...

15:09.570 --> 15:11.700
I'm sorry for bringing this up.

15:11.770 --> 15:12.930
Me, too.

15:13.300 --> 15:15.030
I'm the same as you.

15:15.110 --> 15:17.230
What you said to me made me think...

15:17.410 --> 15:21.440
...about whether I really want to automatically get into our college.

15:23.010 --> 15:27.680
But I'm not in any clubs, and I don't have any hobbies or talents,

15:28.350 --> 15:30.490
so what am I supposed to do?

15:29.390 --> 15:30.490
Kazuki...

15:30.490 --> 15:31.990
Bye-bye, Ikumi!

15:31.390 --> 15:33.390
I'll see you tomorrow, Miss Tachikawa!

15:35.030 --> 15:37.150
Ikumi? Tachikawa?

15:40.830 --> 15:43.800
So, it's you. You're Miss Tachikawa.

15:48.110 --> 15:49.700
M-Mr. Sendou!

15:55.010 --> 15:59.580
250 yen

15:55.010 --> 15:59.580
Crepes

15:55.010 --> 15:59.580
Half Off

15:55.010 --> 15:59.580
Today

15:56.910 --> 15:58.920
What a surprise.

16:00.020 --> 16:02.280
I've met you so many times,

16:02.520 --> 16:06.510
but I never imagined that the Ikumi sending those letters was you.

16:06.660 --> 16:10.090
I'm sorry for writing those letters pretending to act like a grown-up.

16:10.630 --> 16:15.360
I thought that you probably wouldn't take a kid seriously, so I...

16:15.900 --> 16:20.130
So, that's why. But I was really happy to get your fan letters.

16:22.770 --> 16:24.000
Thanks for waiting.

16:25.280 --> 16:26.340
Thanks.

16:26.340 --> 16:27.810
Go ahead, eat.

16:28.250 --> 16:29.740
Thank you very much.

16:32.250 --> 16:33.240
It's delicious!

16:35.690 --> 16:39.020
You sure know a lot about comics, don't you?

16:39.560 --> 16:40.560
Just a while ago,

16:40.560 --> 16:43.930
I was sick and in the hospital for an extended period of time.

16:44.560 --> 16:48.160
I read a lot of comics then, and that's why...

16:48.400 --> 16:51.840
I see. So, are you okay now? Health-wise?

16:52.370 --> 16:54.460
Yes, I'm completely better now.

16:54.670 --> 16:58.010
But you really are amazing, you know that, Mr. Sendou?

16:59.180 --> 17:01.940
When I saw your comic at the spring exhibition and spot sale,

17:02.050 --> 17:05.780
I thought, "This is the comic that I've been looking for!"

17:06.220 --> 17:08.150
Come on, you're exaggerating.

17:09.190 --> 17:10.850
That's not true at all.

17:10.960 --> 17:12.920
I may still be in grade school,

17:13.060 --> 17:15.080
but I am confident in my ability to judge comics.

17:15.960 --> 17:18.260
It's really great to hear you say that, but...

17:18.760 --> 17:23.460
So, what kind of work will you be releasing at the winter Comi-Pa?

17:24.100 --> 17:25.400
Well, that's the thing...

17:26.470 --> 17:29.540
I actually quit doujin work.

17:29.540 --> 17:30.600
What?

17:30.710 --> 17:35.440
A lot happened at the summer
Comi-Pa, so I quit drawing comics.

17:36.850 --> 17:40.580
So, I'm afraid I'm going to have to disappoint you there.

17:42.720 --> 17:46.120
Well, I feel bad after all the letters you wrote me, but...

17:46.620 --> 17:47.890
That's a lie.

17:49.060 --> 17:52.150
Mr. Sendou would never quit drawing comics!

17:52.660 --> 17:53.650
Ikumi...

17:54.300 --> 17:57.360
Mr. Sendou is certain to draw another comic!

17:57.600 --> 18:00.370
To create another wonderful doujinshi!

18:00.640 --> 18:01.470
Ikumi...

18:07.480 --> 18:08.450
I'm sorry.

18:11.720 --> 18:12.940
It isn't dead.

18:14.180 --> 18:16.780
Your art isn't dead yet.

18:16.990 --> 18:18.010
My art?

18:19.320 --> 18:21.420
The sign at the culture fest.

18:25.030 --> 18:27.190
<i>Yes, something very wonderful.</i>

18:27.560 --> 18:30.590
Then the "something wonderful" you were talking about was...

18:31.340 --> 18:33.770
That sign looked really nice.

18:34.200 --> 18:38.040
Your feelings came across loud and clear that you were doing...

18:38.040 --> 18:41.500
...your utmost to draw, not for yourself, but for someone else.

18:43.350 --> 18:44.540
For someone else...

18:48.950 --> 18:52.350
Mr. Sendou is certain to draw another wonderful piece of work.

18:52.990 --> 18:54.550
I have faith in him.

18:56.330 --> 18:59.660
I'm sorry for saying such self-centered things, but...

18:59.830 --> 19:02.320
But I'm your fan, Mr. Sendou.

19:02.600 --> 19:05.590
And I'll always, always be rooting for you!

19:08.870 --> 19:09.810
Ikumi...

19:12.780 --> 19:15.040
Please do your best, Mr. Sendou!

19:24.590 --> 19:26.350
Do my best, huh?

19:26.860 --> 19:28.550
What an earnest girl.

19:28.730 --> 19:29.890
Yeah.

19:29.430 --> 19:31.330
I envy you, Kazuki.

19:31.830 --> 19:34.200
Because what you like to do and want to do...

19:34.260 --> 19:37.260
...leads to other people's enjoyment, and makes them happy.

19:38.740 --> 19:42.400
If only I could lead a life like that, too.

19:43.270 --> 19:44.500
I get it...

19:48.080 --> 19:51.050
So, that's it. That's what it meant!

19:51.920 --> 19:53.510
In other words, that means...

19:54.020 --> 19:58.110
<i>Your feelings came across loud</i> <i>and clear that you were doing...</i>

19:58.320 --> 20:01.290
<i>...your utmost to draw, not for</i> <i>yourself, but for someone else.</i>

20:02.690 --> 20:07.560
<i>As long as there are people lookin'</i> <i>forward to my comics and doujinshi,</i>

20:07.730 --> 20:09.600
<i>I'll never lose the desire to keep doin' it.</i>

20:11.740 --> 20:13.930
<i>But I'm your fan, Mr. Sendou.</i>

20:14.240 --> 20:17.110
<i>And I'll always, always be rooting for you!</i>

20:18.280 --> 20:19.680
Yeah, that's right.

20:25.380 --> 20:27.110
Hey, what's going on?

20:27.680 --> 20:31.120
That's it! That's it! That's how it is!

20:35.230 --> 20:36.320
Kazuki?

20:37.330 --> 20:38.990
I just figured it out!

20:39.260 --> 20:40.130
What?

20:40.130 --> 20:43.290
What I want to do...
No, what I have to do.

20:43.600 --> 20:44.470
Kazuki!

20:44.900 --> 20:47.430
There are people waiting for my comics!

20:47.740 --> 20:49.930
And that's why I have to do it!

20:50.510 --> 20:51.700
Kazuki...

20:54.340 --> 20:57.510
<i>I'll work as hard as I can so</i> <i>that someone out there...</i>

20:57.580 --> 20:59.140
<i>... can enjoy it and have fun with it!</i>

20:59.250 --> 21:01.780
<i>That's what... That's what I want to do!</i>

21:02.290 --> 21:04.520
<i>I don't know about my</i> <i>future or any future,</i>

21:04.820 --> 21:08.850
<i>but right now, I'll work for that</i> <i>someone out there, and for myself...</i>

21:08.930 --> 21:10.290
<i>I'll make doujinshi!</i>

21:10.360 --> 21:11.850
<i>I'll draw comics!</i>

21:49.370 --> 21:50.660
Yeah.

22:20.730 --> 22:24.940
<i>The distant sky looked bright...</i>
<i>Touku no Sora ga Akaruku Mieta</i>

22:24.940 --> 22:29.430
<i>...and we began walking.</i>
<i>Soshite Bokura wa Arukihajimeta</i>

22:29.570 --> 22:33.980
<i>Getting our feet caught in the mud.</i>
<i>Nukarumi ni Ashi o Torarenagara</i>

22:34.140 --> 22:38.050
<i>Heading for a shapeless city.</i>
<i>Katachi no Nai Machi o Mezashite</i>

22:38.050 --> 22:42.150
<i>The pocket in my heart was full...</i>
<i>Kokoro no Naka no Pocket ni wa</i>

22:42.150 --> 22:46.420
<i>...of the grownup things we'd just learned.</i>
<i>Oboetate no Otona ga Ippai</i>

22:46.590 --> 22:51.030
<i>Having taken off our uniforms...</i>
<i>Seifuku o Nuida Bokura ni wa</i>

22:51.160 --> 22:55.170
<i>... the wind was just a little too cold.</i>
<i>Kaze wa Sukoshi Tsumetasugita</i>

22:55.170 --> 22:58.740
<i>Who in the world am I?</i>
<i>Ittai Boku wa Dare Darou</i>

22:58.740 --> 23:03.670
<i>I think about that every so often.</i>
<i>Tokidoki Sonna Koto o Omou</i>

23:03.810 --> 23:07.310
<i>In the world outside the school building...</i>
<i>Kousha no Soto no Sekai de wa</i>

23:07.310 --> 23:12.750
<i>...it's like everyone is a</i> <i>pawn in a game of chess.</i>
<i>Daremo ga Marude Chess no Koma sa</i>

23:13.820 --> 23:18.260
<i>I'm here for you.</i>
<i>Kimi no Tame ni Boku ga Ite</i>

23:18.260 --> 23:22.290
<i>And you for me.</i>
<i>Boku no Tame ni Kimiga</i>

23:22.290 --> 23:26.830
<i>When you think about that...</i>
<i>Sou Omoeba Daremo ga</i>

23:26.830 --> 23:35.800
<i>... everyone is needed by someone.</i>
<i>Dareka no Tame ni Hitsuyou sa</i>

23:56.430 --> 24:20.780
PREVIEW

23:59.360 --> 24:01.130
Taishi, I'm going to do it!

24:01.130 --> 24:04.200
I've decided to give it another try, for my own sake!

24:04.840 --> 24:06.940
Brother 2 is back in business!

24:07.740 --> 24:09.310
Wait, hey, Taishi?

24:09.310 --> 24:10.970
Where did you go?

24:11.640 --> 24:13.180
Is this journal Taishi's?

24:14.280 --> 24:16.510
Kazuki, aim for victory!

24:17.650 --> 24:19.550
T-Taishi, you didn't...

24:20.420 --> 24:23.090
Next time, "Brother 2, Once Again."

24:21.280 --> 24:26.250
NEXT TIME

24:21.280 --> 24:26.250
BROTHER 2,

24:21.280 --> 24:26.250
ONCE AGAIN
